  <title>Budget</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Accounting</gui><gui>Budget</gui></guiseq>: choose a
  <gui>Budget</gui>. There is a row for each month of its fiscal year and a
  column for each budget line, headed with the line's name and monthly amount.
  Each cell is what is left of that line: its monthly amount is added each
  month and what was spent from its account is taken off, carried forward from
  month to month. A negative figure means the line is overspent.
  <gui>Refresh</gui> reads the books again.</p>

  <section id="configure">
  <title>Setting up a budget</title>
  <p>Click <gui>Configure budget</gui>.</p>
  <steps>
    <item><p>To make a budget, type its <gui>Name</gui>, choose the
    <gui>Fiscal</gui> year (see <link xref="fiscal_years"/>) and its
    <gui>Monthly Total</gui>, and click <gui>Add</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Budget</gui> to fill in. For each line, type a
    <gui>Name</gui>, the monthly <gui>Amount</gui>, choose the expense
    <gui>Account</gui> it is spent from, and click <gui>Add</gui>. Click a
    line's amount to change it, or <gui>Remove</gui> it.</p></item>
  </steps>
  <p><gui>Total amount</gui> and <gui>Total percent</gui> show how much of the
  monthly total the lines account for.</p>
  </section>

</page>
